.TH VOLBAR 1 "2026" "Volbar 1.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
volbar \- simple volume bar for X11 desktops
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B volbar
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Volbar is a simple, lightweight volume bar popup for X11 desktops. It displays volume changes with customizable themes, sizes, positions, and slider styles.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Display Options
.TP
.BR \-\-size " \fISIZE\fR"
Window size: small, medium, or large (default: medium)
.TP
.BR \-\-placement " \fIPOS\fR"
Position: center, top, bottom, left, right, top-left, top-right, bottom-left, bottom-right (default: center)
.TP
.BR \-\-icon " on|off"
Show volume icon (default: on)
.TP
.BR \-\-percent " on|off"
Show percentage (default: on)
.TP
.BR \-\-slider " \fITYPE\fR"
Slider style: blocks, dots, line (default: blocks)
.TP
.BR \-\-theme " \fINAME\fR"
Theme name from ~/.config/volbar/themes/ (default: default)
.TP
.BR \-\-timeout " \fIMS\fR"
Display timeout in milliseconds (default: 2000)
.SS Daemon Options
.TP
.BR \-\-start\-daemon
Start background monitoring daemon
.TP
.BR \-\-stop\-daemon
Stop running daemon
.TP
.BR \-\-poll\-interval " \fIMS\fR"
Volume check interval for daemon mode in milliseconds (default: 200)
.SS System Tray Options
.TP
.BR \-\-systray\-icon
Enable system tray volume control (X11 only)
.TP
.BR \-\-tray\-step " \fIN\fR"
Volume step per scroll (default: 5)
.TP
.BR \-\-mixer " \fICMD\fR"
Mixer command for tray menu (default: pavucontrol)
.SS Other Options
.TP
.BR \-\-debug
Enable debug output
.TP
.BR \-\-list\-themes
List available themes
.TP
.BR \-\-list\-sliders
List available slider styles
.TP
.BR \-\-test\-themes
Preview all themes with current volume
.TP
.BR \-\-show
Show volume once and exit (default mode)
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display help message
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Display version information
.SH SLIDER STYLES
.TP
.B blocks
█████░░░░░ (default)
.TP
.B dots
●●●●●○○○○○
.TP
.B line
━━━━━─────
.SH EXAMPLES
Show volume bar:
.RS
.B volbar \-\-show
.RE
.PP
Show with custom theme and placement:
.RS
.B volbar \-\-show \-\-placement top-right \-\-theme nord
.RE
.PP
Show with line slider style:
.RS
.B volbar \-\-show \-\-slider line
.RE
.PP
Start daemon mode:
.RS
.B volbar \-\-start\-daemon \-\-placement top-right
.RE
.PP
Start daemon with system tray:
.RS
.B volbar \-\-start\-daemon \-\-systray-icon
.RE
.PP
Start daemon with faster polling:
.RS
.B volbar \-\-start\-daemon \-\-poll\-interval 100
.RE
.PP
List available sliders:
.RS
.B volbar \-\-list\-sliders
.RE
.PP
Stop daemon:
.RS
.B volbar \-\-stop\-daemon
.RE
.SH THEMES
Themes are CSS files stored in user or system directories.
.PP
To create a custom theme, create a CSS file in
.I ~/.config/volbar/themes/
with the following structure:
.PP
.RS
.nf
#volbar-container {
    background-color: #1a1a1a;
    border: 2px solid #00ff00;
    border-radius: 8px;
}

label#icon { color: #00ff00; }
label#slider { color: #00ff00; }
label#percentage { color: #ffffff; }

label#icon.muted,
label#slider.muted,
label#percentage.muted { color: #ff0000; }
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/volbar/themes/
User theme directory
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/volbar/themes/
System theme directory
.TP
.I ~/.cache/volbar.pid
Daemon PID file
.SH AUDIO BACKENDS
Volbar auto-detects audio backends in this order:
.IP 1. 3
PipeWire (wpctl)
.IP 2. 3
PulseAudio (pactl)
.IP 3. 3
ALSA (amixer)
.SH DAEMON MODE
When running in daemon mode, volbar monitors volume changes by polling the audio backend at the interval specified by
.BR \-\-poll\-interval .
.PP
Lower values (e.g., 100ms) provide more responsive feedback but use slightly more CPU.
Higher values (e.g., 500ms) reduce CPU usage but may feel laggy.
.PP
The default of 200ms works well for most users.
.SH SYSTEM TRAY
When
.B \-\-systray-icon
is enabled, volbar adds a status icon to the system tray.
.PP
.IP \(bu 2
Scroll up/down to adjust volume
.IP \(bu 2
Left-click or middle-click to toggle mute
.IP \(bu 2
Right-click for menu (mixer, quit)
